# November 28, 2026: state hospitals and asylums of Georgia, Alabama, Mississippi, Louisiana, Arkansas and Florida, a
# batch of the themed pass on historic state hospitals. Searcy Hospital at Mount Vernon, Alabama, was already on the map
# (with the Mount Vernon Arsenal) and is not added again.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's articles on each institution; the Park Service's National Register records
# and forms (the Central Building at Milledgeville and its cemeteries, the Alabama Insane Hospital, the Center Building at
# Jackson, Louisiana, the Chattahoochee arsenal, Rose Cottage and the dairy barn at Pineville); the New Georgia
# Encyclopedia, the Georgia Trust, Visit Milledgeville and news reports on Central State Hospital; SAH Archipedia, the
# Encyclopedia of Alabama, the University of Alabama's building pages and the Alabama Department of Mental Health's museum
# page; Mississippi State Hospital's own history page, SAH Archipedia and the University of Mississippi Medical Center,
# Smithsonian, Archaeology and Clarion Ledger reports on Asylum Hill; Asylum Projects for East Mississippi State
# Hospital; 64 Parishes; the Louisiana Department of Health; the Encyclopedia of Arkansas; Clio; Historic Augusta; the
# Ellisville State School's own page; and HMdb's transcriptions of state and society markers. Asylum Projects was used only
# for what nothing else gave, and the text says so. No patient is named. Pins: Register and Wikipedia points, address
# lookups and OpenStreetMap features, every one looked at on the aerial.
